# Canonical -> vendored destinations for the shared A2A wire code (QUAL-4).
#
# Format: <file-in-a2a_common/>  <dest-dir> [<dest-dir> ...]
# Blank lines and #-comments ignored. Read by BOTH scripts/ci/sync-a2a-core.sh
# and scripts/ci/hygiene-check.sh — keep it the single list.
#
# Only files that are ALREADY byte-identical across their consumers belong here.
# A file that legitimately differs per service (client.py, mount.py, the
# authority_*/partner_*/sdk_* modules) is NOT shared code and must not be added.
#
# SCOPE: destinations in THIS repository only. The partner platform keeps its own
# copies in its own repository  and
# validates them with its own CI. Nothing here can see or check those copies, so
# hmac_signer.py staying byte-identical across the A2A trust boundary is a
# release-coordination responsibility — see CONTRIBUTING.md.

# certagent/{cert-agent,bank-agent} were destinations before the certification
# stacks moved to the oss-a2a-platform repository. Listing a path that does not
# exist here makes sync-a2a-core.sh abort before it reaches protocol.py, so the
# gate silently stopped covering the other two files. Re-add them only alongside
# the trees themselves.
hmac_signer.py    backend/app/a2a_common
protocol.py       backend/app/a2a_common
executor_base.py  backend/app/a2a_common

# The integration-testing tunnel's contract and alias allowlist. Vendored for
# the same reason as the three above: both platforms must agree byte-for-byte,
# and the allowlist is the SSRF control on that tunnel — a copy that drifts
# reopens the hole on one side only.
integration_contract.py   backend/app/a2a_common
integration_allowlist.py  backend/app/a2a_common
